-- Cheaper Cooldown Haste and Proc Chance (level60-stat-curve S21, user ruling 2026-11-22): Cooldown Haste costs 6
-- rating per 1% at level 60 (was 14, 1:1 with Crit since LS3) and Proc Chance 4 (was 7, half of Crit's rating), so a
-- bracket's top gear reaches about 70-80% Cooldown Haste and about 105% Proc Chance. Both stay tied to the Crit curve
-- at every level: CR_COOLDOWN_HASTE (CR 22) rows 2200-2299 = CR_CRIT_SPELL (CR 10) rows 1000-1099 x 6/14, and
-- CR_PROC_CHANCE (CR 11) rows 1100-1199 = CR 10 x 4/14. Item budgets still price both ratings equal to Crit.
-- `gtoctclasscombatratingscalar_dbc` needs nothing (CR 11 and CR 22 are a flat 1 for every class). Each UPDATE
-- guards on the old value (float tolerance, the column is FLOAT), so a re-run or a hand-edited row is a no-op; this
-- file sorts after rev_cooldown_haste_1to1_crit.sql, whose CR 22 values it expects. Regenerate patch-Y at deploy
-- (apps/dbc-tools/patch_gt_tables.py covers CR 11 and CR 22 through lib/gt_dbc.py's CUSTOM_COMBAT_RATINGS).
